{"resourceIdentifier":"4367","resourceName":"Zhenyuan Swine Farm AWMS GHG Mitigation Project","description":"Zhenyuan Swine Farm AWMS GHG Mitigation Project (hereinafter referred to as the Project) introduces 1 new animal waste management system (AWMS) to treat the manure from the existing swine farm in Zhenyuan County, Guizhou Province, which are owned by ZHENYUAN XINMU Agricultural Development Co., Ltd (hereinafter called the project owner). Each subsidiary swine farm will install one AWMS. The purpose of the project activity is to treat the manure and wastewater to avoid methane emissions generated in the baseline uncovered anaerobic lagoons.\r\nThe common practice for local swine farm owners to manage the manure is to have uncovered anaerobic lagoons/ponds at their farms in the region. As per “technical specification for sanitation treatment of livestock and poultry manure ”, in China, the uncovered anaerobic lagoons are a manure treatment method recognized by the state. In addition, since there is no legal regulation to mandate the livestock farm owners to implement anaerobic digestion, aerobic or other biological treatment techniques and to capture and/or utilize methane generated at their lagoons, therefore the continue of this common practice to treatment the manure i.e., uncovered anaerobic lagoons is the most economic, viable and reasonable for livestock farm owners.\r\nIt is estimated that approximately 388.64*104 m3 of biogas will be produced annually. The biogas will be captured and utilized for heat generation, the heat will be only used for the daily operation of the AWMS and the swine farm and will not be produced to other users. For conservativeness, baseline emissions from heat generation are neglected.\r\nThe project activity will reduce of GHG in the atmosphere through avoiding methane emissions from anaerobic treatment of swine manure and wastewater. It is estimated that 32,028 tCO2e emission reductions will be produced annually.","location":{"latitude":27.350435,"longitude":108.215906},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-07-24","endExclusive":"2023-08-24","endInclusive":"2023-08-23"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4367"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Guizhou"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Multiple Proponents"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"4367"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"36193"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Livestock, enteric fermentation, and manure management"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ACM0010"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"CTI Certification Co., Ltd."}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"14/11/2024"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 11/12/2021 - 10/12/2028"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=88567&IDKEY=ciofj09234rm9oq4jndsma80vcalksdjf98cxkjaf90823nmq3v122133893","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"VCS_PD_Zhenyuan New Hope_20230419_draft.pdf","uploadDate":"2023-04-19T07:20:17.5Z"},{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=88962&IDKEY=3iquwesdfmnk0iei23nnm435oiojnc909dsflk9809adlkmlkfj122678598","documentType":"Listing Representation","documentName":"Listing-Representation-Multiple-Representors.pdf","uploadDate":"2023-04-26T03:31:53.63Z"}]},{"code":"VCS_REGISTRATION_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Registration Documents","documents":[{"uri":"